er for the Commonwealth to pay the claimant the market value of the goods at the time they were disposed of or destroyed, if they have been disposed of or destroyed before the end of the proceedings; or  (iii) a declaration that the goods are not forfeited.  (5) For the purposes of subsection (4), if the proceedings go to judgment, they end:  (a) at the end of the period for lodging an appeal against the judgment, if no appeal is lodged within that period; or  (b) when the appeal lapses or is finally determined, if an appeal is lodged against the judgment within that period.  (6) For the purposes of this section, the return of goods requires their return to the person reasonably believed to be the owner of the goods in a condition as near as practicable to the condition in which they were seized." ;
    cof:pageNumber "15"^^xsd:integer .

