concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "16 At the end of section 360.4 of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-16 ;
    values:originalText "Add:  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory that makes:  (a) an act or omission that is an offence against this Division; or  (b) a similar act or omission; an offence against the law of the State or Territory. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Firearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2  No. 12, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other Measures) Act 2015  (3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does any one or more of the following:  (a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the penalty provided for in this Division;  (b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that differs from the fault elements applicable to the offence against this Division;  (c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs from the defences applicable to the offence against this Division.  (4) A person punished for an offence against a law of a State or Territory referred to in subsection (2) in respect of particular conduct cannot be punished for an offence against this Division in respect of that conduct." ;
    skos:definition "Add:  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), this Division is not intended to exclude or limit the concurrent operation of a law of a State or Territory that makes:  (a) an act or omission that is an offence against this Division; or  (b) a similar act or omission; an offence against the law of the State or Territory. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Firearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2  No. 12, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other Measures) Act 2015  (3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does any one or more of the following:  (a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the penalty provided for in this Division;  (b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that differs from the fault elements applicable to the offence against this Division;  (c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs from the defences applicable to the offence against this Division.  (4) A person punished for an offence against a law of a State or Territory referred to in subsection (2) in respect of particular conduct cannot be punished for an offence against this Division in respect of that conduct."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-16-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
