    values:originalText "(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does any one or more of the following:  (a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the penalty provided for in this Division;  (b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that differs from the fault elements applicable to the offence against this Division;  (c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs from the defences applicable to the offence against this Division." ;
    skos:definition "(3) Subsection (2) applies even if the law of the State or Territory does any one or more of the following:  (a) provides for a penalty for the offence that differs from the penalty provided for in this Division;  (b) provides for a fault element in relation to the offence that differs from the fault elements applicable to the offence against this Division;  (c) provides for a defence in relation to the offence that differs from the defences applicable to the offence against this Division."@en ;
