concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-2-sec-361-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "361 4  Defence—reasonable belief that conduct is justified or excused"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-2-sec-361-4 ;
    values:originalText "by or under a law  A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against this Division if:  (a) at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the person was under a mistaken but reasonable belief that the conduct was justified or excused by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Firearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2  No. 12, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other Measures) Act 2015  (b) had the conduct been so justified or excused—the conduct would not have constituted the offence. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in paragraph (a) (see subsection 13.3(3))." ;
    skos:definition "by or under a law  A person is not criminally responsible for an offence against this Division if:  (a) at the time of the conduct constituting the offence, the person was under a mistaken but reasonable belief that the conduct was justified or excused by or under a law of the Commonwealth or of a State or Territory; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Firearms trafficking offences  Schedule 2  No. 12, 2015 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Psychoactive Substances and Other Measures) Act 2015  (b) had the conduct been so justified or excused—the conduct would not have constituted the offence. Note: A defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to the matter in paragraph (a) (see subsection 13.3(3))."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "3023817330ed1e46393424e00330ff09935d9b0a9cea0770f173665c92306d3f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defence—reasonable belief that conduct is justified or excused" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf> ;
