concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-10a a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "10A Decisions by the Attorney-General about transfers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-10a ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Attorney-General need not take any steps for making:  (a) a decision on an application under section 16 (about transfers from Australia) for the transfer of a prisoner; or  (b) a decision under section 24 (about transfers to Australia) about a request for the transfer of a prisoner; if any of the following requirements for the transfer are not met:  (c) paragraph 10(a), (c), (e) or (f);  (d) paragraph 10(b), to the extent that it requires the agreement of the transfer country to the transfer;  (e) paragraph 10(d), to the extent that it requires the consent of State Ministers or Territory Ministers to the transfer. Note: The prisoner will be kept informed about the progress of the application or request (see section 52).  (2) The Attorney-General need not take any steps for making a decision referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) for the transfer of a prisoner if:  (a) the prisoner had made an earlier application or request; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Schedule 3  International transfer of prisoners" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Attorney-General need not take any steps for making:  (a) a decision on an application under section 16 (about transfers from Australia) for the transfer of a prisoner; or  (b) a decision under section 24 (about transfers to Australia) about a request for the transfer of a prisoner; if any of the following requirements for the transfer are not met:  (c) paragraph 10(a), (c), (e) or (f);  (d) paragraph 10(b), to the extent that it requires the agreement of the transfer country to the transfer;  (e) paragraph 10(d), to the extent that it requires the consent of State Ministers or Territory Ministers to the transfer. Note: The prisoner will be kept informed about the progress of the application or request (see section 52).  (2) The Attorney-General need not take any steps for making a decision referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) for the transfer of a prisoner if:  (a) the prisoner had made an earlier application or request; and ComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00012  Schedule 3  International transfer of prisoners"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "be000936054f65657e12a5a5ed5999eb804cadfca275708bace36f27f3563a5c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "33"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-10a-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-3-sec-10a-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.33" .
