doc:sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "270(1) 3B  Prosecutions" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Proceedings for an offence against section 270.3, where the conduct constituting the alleged offence occurs wholly outside Australia, must not take place except with the consent in writing of the Attorney-General." ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "270(2) 3B  Prosecutions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-4-sec-270-2-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not been given in relation to an offence against section 270.3:  (a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for the arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and executed; and  (b) a person may be charged with the offence; and  (c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail; but no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to be taken until such a consent has been given." ;
    skos:definition "(2) Even though a consent in accordance with subsection (1) has not been given in relation to an offence against section 270.3:  (a) a person may be arrested for the offence, and a warrant for the arrest of a person for the offence may be issued and executed; and  (b) a person may be charged with the offence; and  (c) a person so charged may be remanded in custody or on bail; but no further step in proceedings referred to in subsection (1) is to be taken until such a consent has been given."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "23f75aa1b9359f08c8f8ff694f76fb7a3c8be87927eff5adab5183527abd916d" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-psychoactive-substances-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-4-sec-270-2 ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
